X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96079341819709

Thanks to Bryan Lavell, Rodrigo Poblete, Emmanual, Matthias, Dolder, Anthony
Miller, Viktor Holmbert, Raja Nagaraja, Martin Moore, Eskil Swahn, Nikola
Milutinovic, Frank Wortner, alan@nabeth.cxo.dec.com, and Dr. Tom Blinn for
their responses.

The answer was that the OS needs to be upgraded first (minimum 4.0e, though
those that mentioned it, suggested 4.0f minimum) because 4.0d is not able to
run on an EV6 processor.

Dr. Blinn also suggested that we might be well off to either upgrade to a
Wildfire when they come out, or that we might get as much bang for our buck
if we went with an ES40 instead of the GS60.

Thank you all.

John


