Hi,
the solution was fairly simple and to be honest pretty obvious ... the
"cannot
open Display (hostname) was the key"  .... I could log in using
the IP address but not the hostname ... the box uses NIS and the /etc/hosts
file was been populated and not the /var/yp/src/host so when the CDE was
looking for the hostname it could not find it  ..

I've now populated the /var/yp/src/hosts with all the correct IP/hosts and
the
login now works ok

Thanks to Hank Lee and Kevin Partin for responding

Tony.

extract from Kevin Partin
>
In /var/dt/Xconfig, set

###########################################################################
#
#  To disable R4 MIT-MAGIC-COOKIE-1 per-user authorization.
#
Dtlogin*authorize:         False

This should allow logins. You may have to restart the Xserver.
====

extract from Hank Lee
>
Perhaps they would try a completitive project. We use WRQ Reflection X
here,
and it seems to work just fine. (no special setup needed on the UNIX box) I
believe their web page is http://www.wrq.com.


