To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: LSM mirror synchronization
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96079341819386

We use LSM to mirror volumes across ESA10000s.  On Friday, we had a system
crash.  Everything came up fine, but processing was extremely slow the rest
of the day due to the LSM mirrors re-synchronizing.  Is there anyway to
inhibit/stop the resynching until non-prime hours?  Or maybe lower the
priority?  Obviously, you want to get things synchronized ASAP, but
management is concerned about the impact on production. (Never mind if you
lose a disk that's not yet mirrored!)

